A||||3||Brian84SE||Brake relay?||||1||
Z||000000||Brian84SE||03-05-2000||08:19 PM||||Every time I apply the brakes, I hear a clicking in the engine compartment as the brake lights come on.  It doesnt matter whether the engine is on or not.  Is there a  relay that controls the brake lights?  The haynes manual doesnt seem to show one....||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||03-05-2000||08:43 PM||||Are you sure it's not coming from the calipers/rotors etc?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||03-05-2000||09:09 PM||||I assume from your name that you have an 84. If so, then you do have 2 relays in the engine compartment that operate the outboard stop/turn signal lights!  If you raise the trunk lid and look on the firewall in front of the air cleaner snorkel you will see four little black boxes with wires on them.  One is the fuel pump relay, one is (I believe)the a/c clutch relay, and the other two are the stop/turn signal relays, one for the left outboard bulb and one for the right outboard bulb.  I have no idea why GM uses this system, the relays do not control the other bulbs in the tail lights, just the very outboard bulb on each side!?!?  I had one relay get sticky and found only 1 bulb still lit after parking the car.  Took a while to figure that one out!!||||reg||10
Z||000003||Cooter||03-05-2000||11:37 PM||||If you have cruise control, it could be the vac. bleed off solinoid (sp???)||||reg||1
